        "original_id": "518bd885-f55e-5e8f-a120-e6130963efcc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Stein, Charles Russell, Bob Engelman, Mike Werb, Mary Alice Stephenson\n- Films: Ferris Bueller's Day Off, The Mask, Son of the Mask\n- Television Shows: America's Most Smartest Model\n- Roles: economics teacher, Dr. Arthur Neuman\n- Organizations: Dark Horse Comics\n- Concepts: comic series adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, Ben Stein appeared on screen as the economics teacher in \"Ferris Bueller's Day Off.\"\n- In 1994, \"The Mask\" was released as an American superhero fantasy comedy film.\n- In 1994, \"The Mask\" was directed by Charles Russell, produced by Bob Engelman, and written by Mike Werb.\n- In 1994, \"The Mask\" was based on the comic series of the same name distributed by Dark Horse Comics.\n- In 1994, Ben Stein played Dr. Arthur Neuman in \"The Mask.\"\n- In 2005, Ben Stein played Dr. Arthur Neuman in \"Son of the Mask.\"\n- Ben Stein and Mary Alice Stephenson were the hosts of \"America's Most Smartest Model.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
